{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/275143-how-many-of-x-are-there","id":275143,"title":"How many of X are there ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-07T19:50:14-07:00","id":275143,"title":"How many of X are there ?","content":"I was discussing with one of my players about the characters in the WoD and i mentioned how L.A doenst have more than a dozen of kindread and he was surprised.<br /> that got me to think, How many (canon) of each there is in the world of darkness. it doesnt work if i tell you that one third of 9.999.999.999 of the angels are stuck in the abysm, but rather how many they are on earth at the moment (aprox)<br /> <br /> I was told that Vampires were around the 1.500 around the world, 2 vampires every 500 humans or something a like (sorry im bad at math)<br /> <br /> as for Hunters i belive theres about 600 (mentioned in Hunter net), but operative/alive i would go as far as to say 200<br /> <br /> Demons, i belive the largest concentration of them is in L.A and they are about 81 (not counting lucifer or the supposed 666 earthbounds on earth, taking the numbers from the L.A and Fear to Thread books)<br /> <br /> I have No idea how many Changelings there are in general but i was told that theres like one every 1.000 humans (at least on earth, not in arcadia)<br /> <br /> Wraiths on earth, they have the biggest numbers id magine, concidering all the ghost stories and whatnot.<br /> <br /> Mages, i would hardly belive if theres more than 300 in the entire world.<br /> <br /> Werewolves: no idea how many they would be, but im pretty sure that they are the fewer. since they are...sort of meant to loose the war against the Wyrm, and i belive there was no more than 50 on earth (at least thats what my ST told me)<br /> <br /> All i know on the WW side is that theres 300 nuwisha total, and only 100 are allowed on earth at the same time. no idea how many shapeshifters theres on earth. specially since The Purgue that was the Rage War.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T05:48:42-07:00","id":275411,"title":"","content":"The supernatural demography of oWoD varies a lot...<br /> Vampire's storyteller handbook 2ed says that there were one vampire for each 100.000 humans. But I'm informed that there are more generous ciphers, like a vampire for each 10.000 humans.<br /> <br /> There are supposed to be one mage for each 1000.000 humans or one mage for each 250.000, with more generous numbers. Also, in Hidden Lore it's stated that there are around 2000-10.000 mages in the world. Follow the link for an interesting reflection on the matter: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...the-traditions</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-08-2014, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T06:39:54-07:00","id":275428,"title":"","content":"There are, of course, no definite answers to this. The general guidelines gleaned from the various lines are something like this:<br /> <br /> Kindred: About 1: 100.000 in Camarilla controlled areas, as this is their guideline, about twice that in Anarch or Sabbat controlled areas. So something like 70-100 000 vampires in all.<br /> <br /> Garou: About 1: 500.000, which gives about 35 000 Garou worldwide.<br /> <br /> Fera: Uncertain. Some breeds are nigh extinct while others like Ratkin are more numerous than any one Garou Tribe.<br /> <br /> Mages: About 1: 1 000 000, giving about 7000 Mages worldwide<br /> <br /> Fallen: As many as have managed to squeeze through the cracks<br /> <br /> Edit: I need to check up on my Fera numbers again","signature":"","edited":{"userid":300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","user":"HOD","date":". 10-08-2014, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T08:56:34-07:00","id":275476,"title":"","content":"I liked the &quot;WtA Storytellers Handbook&quot; answer most - <b>Not enough</b>.<br /> <br /> Also, I can't really remember where comes the information, that Mage is 1 in million. There were about 150-200 awakened members of <i>each</i> Craft (with some exceptions), and they've been considered to be smaller then proper Traditions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","name":"von Lyttenburgh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3479_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T08:58:12-07:00","id":275479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HOD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/275143-how-many-of-x-are-there?p=275428#post275428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages: About 1: 1 000 000, giving about 7000 Mages worldwide</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that as Aleph said, the one in a million was changed later.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T10:17:05-07:00","id":275564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/275143-how-many-of-x-are-there?p=275476#post275476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the &quot;WtA Storytellers Handbook&quot; answer most - <b>Not enough</b>.<br /> <br /> Also, I can't really remember where comes the information, that Mage is 1 in million. There were about 150-200 awakened members of <i>each</i> Craft (with some exceptions), and they've been considered to be smaller then proper Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm remembering correctly, the <i>Book of Crafts</i> talked about the Bata'a rivaling the size of some of the Traditions with about 400 awakened mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T11:24:11-07:00","id":275606,"title":"","content":"The most important statistic - how many humans there are in the CWOD.<br /> <br /> 5. It's one family that lives in the middle of Kansas. They've never experienced the supernatural world in any way, shape or form. They are not ghouls, kinfolk, kinain, mediums, hunters, etc, etc, etc. The only truly mundane people in the whole world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 10-08-2014, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T11:40:33-07:00","id":275639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only truly mundane people in the whole world. </div> </div> </div>I thought only Hitler was one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T12:03:50-07:00","id":275650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/275143-how-many-of-x-are-there?p=275639#post275639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought only Hitler was one.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct that he was one, but the only dead people we are counting are vampires, wraiths and mummies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T12:38:26-07:00","id":275672,"title":"","content":"There are no mundanes anymore then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T14:20:24-07:00","id":275737,"title":"","content":"Clanbook:Giovanni Revisited estimates the number of Kindred to be at most forty thousand.<br /> Seventy thousand would be too many, if we consider the Kuei-Jin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3117-lucius","name":"Lucius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T14:31:10-07:00","id":275768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lucius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/275143-how-many-of-x-are-there?p=275737#post275737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clanbook:Giovanni Revisited estimates the number of Kindred to be at most forty thousand.<br /> Seventy thousand would be too many, if we consider the Kuei-Jin.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Clanbook Giovanni rev. was published in 2001. The world has almost 1 billion more people now. That wold equal 10k vampires.<br /> <br /> 2. The Kuei-Jin were included in my estimates, you're correct, I should have used &quot;vampires&quot;, not Kindred. If you exclude the parts of the world where they are, you would lower the total population by some 2-3 billion people (China itself is 1.3), thus reducing the number with 20-30k.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T10:19:21-07:00","id":276452,"title":"","content":"I operate under the assumption there is 60 thousand kindred and 2 thousand of them are members of bloodlines. There is a malkavian conspiracy theorist who believes the number stays constant since every time one dies a new kindred always seems to arrive to replace the decease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1244-starsoverstalingrad","name":"StarsOverStalingrad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1244_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T05:52:50-07:00","id":277127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/275143-how-many-of-x-are-there?p=275606#post275606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most important statistic - how many humans there are in the CWOD.<br /> <br /> 5. It's one family that lives in the middle of Kansas. They've never experienced the supernatural world in any way, shape or form. They are not ghouls, kinfolk, kinain, mediums, hunters, etc, etc, etc. The only truly mundane people in the whole world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their last name wouldn't be &quot;Kent&quot; now would it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T16:04:06-07:00","id":277660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/275143-how-many-of-x-are-there?p=277127#post277127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Their last name wouldn't be &quot;Kent&quot; now would it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironicly, no. Caine is the family name. Seth Caine is the father. Go figure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T11:18:33-07:00","id":279910,"title":"","content":"Including the Thallain, Nunnehi and Dauntain I use 1 &quot;Changeling&quot; for every 20,000. Technocracy writes they're almost extinct? It's true, their impact on humanity is almost nothing, they lost the consensual reality and their reincarnation cycles are finite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3920-sarah-rps","name":"Sarah RPs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T07:03:59-07:00","id":282236,"title":"","content":"Uh, it's still more than Garou and Vampires, so it's not almost extinct.<br /> <br /> For one, I use Lost Changelings, so their numbers depend on how many people break away from Gentry. Reality is poisoning Gentry because of Consensus but they are nearly untouchable within Arcadia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T18:27:30-07:00","id":283014,"title":"","content":"I think the reason that everyone considers Changeling &quot;almost extinct&quot; is because of the Mists. Since everyone forgets, and they don't generally have a large overall impact to draw attention, people think they aren't around. Any high banality people are going to have no memory of having interacted with them, so Technocracy numbers for them are logically going to be pretty far off.<br /> Finally found this again. This information is what I generally used for the various splat populations: <a href=\"http://z6.invisionfree.com/Masquerade_Project/index.php?showtopic=1376\" target=\"_blank\">http://z6.invisionfree.com/Masquerad...showtopic=1376</a><br /> And I acknowledge that the human population has gone up and numbers may have to be adjusted some.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T08:30:21-07:00","id":283875,"title":"","content":"The Changeling impact is gone. They can yell all they want, but they lost and the Technocracy, I believe, made that statement with regards to their measured effect on the consensual reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3920-sarah-rps","user":"Sarah RPs","date":". 10-16-2014, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3920-sarah-rps","name":"Sarah RPs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T12:34:25-07:00","id":285205,"title":"","content":"Just a sidemark, but at this point I should rename my port in works of Technocracy and its Conventions to NWoD, because they veered off too much from their OWoD counterpart. It all started with them being non-Mages, just people researching scraps of God-Machine lore (including 'angel skeletons') for betterment of common man and it all ended up with things like Void Engineers being comrade-in-arms with Summer Courts against Gentry incursions and other conventions (no Progenitor equivalent, we have Cheiron already) being pretty chill about their new allies. <br /> <br /> Kind of contrast to Technocracy's dismissal. Especially that Changelings are precious auxiliaries as FTL travel leads through Hedge as a shortcut. <br /> <br /> And Dauntain have now equivalent in my semi-homebrew Iron Court (since I want to develop that from a premise I found at /tg/). They are Spocks to generally more passionate Changelings, but can be pretty bro tier (just like Vulkans) even if they are in denial and strive for highest Clarity possible. <br /> <br /> Klingons are now Ogre Kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}